<svg class="dg" viewBox="0 0 1100 712" role="img" aria-labelledby="dg-title dg-desc">
<title id="dg-title">How Sub-Sub works</title>
<desc id="dg-desc">You use Sub-Sub in the browser view or in the terminal. Sub-Sub runs in pi on your computer and sends your messages to the model provider that you choose. The mode decides which servers it may use: the librarian reads and changes the library through the zotero server; the researcher reads the library through the zotero server and uses the scholar server and, if it is on, the verify server (Starbuck). The profile removes tools from either mode. Every library change goes through the approval gate. The zotero server talks to Zotero on 127.0.0.1 and keeps a journal of changes for undo. The servers use online services such as PubMed, Europe PMC, OpenAlex, Crossref, Unpaywall and Open Library. Sub-Sub writes notes in your notes folder and reads its settings from your configuration folder.</desc>
